  "boundaries": [
    "Original application and vendor production source plus additive controls reproduce late type-size and ineligible-topic admission. The tiny fixtures create no network connections.",
    "Static twelve-topic whitelist covers all six supported repository fork/BPO digest states. Existing active/pre/retiring policy and all cryptographic verification remain unchanged.",
    "Receive, GRAFT, PRUNE and codec-invalid gates use the documented expanded can_subscribe eligibility hook. AllowAll behavior is preserved; mutable/custom cardinality filters are explicitly not treated as equivalent policies.",
    "Existing per-type compressed/decoded limits run before message IDs/cache insertion. The message-ID algorithm, including bounded malformed Snappy, is unchanged.",
    "All 34 upstream package files and exact reconstruction of the six modified files were checked. CI retains expiry coverage and adds topic controls; no dependency version or lockfile changed.",
    "Initial RPC decoding and generic transform cloning precede the type guard. No total RSS/cache/queue cap or measured throughput improvement is claimed.",
    "Protected metadata, eligible cache admission/overload policy, priority control queues, shared query resources, dashboard, verified repair and integrated acceptance remain open.",
    "No benchmark, live sync, production data, remote-host work or release-readiness claim."
